  "Groups": [
    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "NOT1",
        "Description": "NOT reading (input A, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.375) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the load-enabled bit: select inversion, Y = NOT(Load), feeding NANDA.B \u2014 the hold arm of the multiplexer in front of the register. The fan-out of Load onto NOT1 and NANDB happens at the logic layer: both unconnected pins share the persisted signal name Load, so one network toggle drives them without a waveguide. The whole bit composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here.",
        "Identifier": "group_7a2223163d864b6a94a79dca3aeb6421",
        "IdGuid": "993d79f5-8399-4fb8-bff2-e5eb6dd506cd",
